  }

  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; }
  .wrap {
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding: clamp(20px, 4vw, 56px);
    min-height: 100vh;
  }
  .page { max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; }

  header { margin-bottom: 34px; }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent); margin: 0 0 10px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(24px, 4vw, 34px); line-height: 1.15; margin: 0 0 10px;
    letter-spacing: -.015em; text-wrap: balance; font-weight: 650;
  }
  .lede { margin: 0; max-width: 62ch; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; }
  .lede b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }

  /* flow spine */
  .node {
    background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px;
  }
  .req {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px;
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-soft);
    background: var(--surface); border: 1px dashed var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: 999px; padding: 7px 15px;
  }
  .req b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .drop { width: 2px; background: var(--line-strong); margin: 10px 0; height: 22px; }
  .center { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; }

  .master { text-align: center; width: 100%; max-width: 460px; border-color: var(--line-strong); }
  .master .name { font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 650; font-size: 16px; }
  .master .sub { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 13px; margin-top: 3px; }

  .router-label {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11.5px; letter-spacing: .06em;
    color: var(--ink-soft); text-transform: uppercase;
    margin: 12px 0 4px; text-align: center;
  }

  /* branches */
  .branches {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px;
    margin-top: 22px; align-items: start;
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .branches { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  .branch {
    background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 14px; overflow: hidden; display: flex; flex-direction: column;
  }
  .branch .cap { height: 4px; }
  .b1 .cap { background: var(--accent); }
  .b2 .cap { background: var(--iss); }
  .b3 .cap { background: var(--legacy); }

  .branch .body { padding: 16px 17px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 11px; }
  .branch .top { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; }
  .num {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700;
    width: 22px; height: 22px; border-radius: 6px; flex: none;
    display: grid; place-items: center; color: #fff;
  }
  .b1 .num { background: var(--accent); }
  .b2 .num { background: var(--iss); }
  .b3 .num { background: var(--legacy); }
  .branch h3 { margin: 0; font-size: 14.5px; font-weight: 650; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  .branch .where { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--ink-soft); }

  .tag {
    align-self: flex-start; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10.5px;
    letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 600;
    padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 999px;
  }
  .tag.fast { background: var(--accent-soft); color: var(--accent-ink); }
  .tag.native { background: var(--iss-soft); color: var(--iss); }
  .tag.rest { background: var(--legacy-soft); color: var(--legacy); }

  .kv { font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink); }
  .kv .k { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .04em;
           text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft); display: block; margin-bottom: 1px; }
  .kv code, .oids { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12.5px; }
  .oids { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6; }

  /* iss_build routing table inside branch 3 */
  .rt-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin-top: 2px; }
  table.rt { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 12.5px; }
  table.rt th, table.rt td { text-align: left; padding: 7px 9px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  table.rt thead th { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: .05em;
                      text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft); font-weight: 600; }
  table.rt td.cond { font-family: var(--mono); color: var(--legacy); white-space: nowrap; }
  table.rt tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
  .to-fw { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }
  .to-iss { color: var(--iss); font-weight: 600; }

  /* migration callout */
  .callout {
    margin-top: 26px; background: var(--accent-soft); border: 1px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 12px; padding: 15px 18px; display: flex; gap: 14px; align-items: flex-start;
  }
  .callout .arrow { font-family: var(--mono); color: var(--accent-ink); font-weight: 700; font-size: 15px; }
  .callout p { margin: 0; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--ink); }
  .callout b { color: var(--accent-ink); }

  .foot { margin-top: 22px; padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
          font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--ink-soft); display: grid; gap: 6px; }
  .foot code { font-family: var(--mono); color: var(--ink); }
  .foot .pin { color: var(--iss); font-weight: 600; }
</style>

<div class="wrap"><div class="page">
  <header>
    <p class="eyebrow">Plan D · MDS-G4000-L3-4XGS</p>
    <h1>SNMP request routing — current architecture</h1>
    <p class="lede">The snmpd master fans each request out by OID. <b>Design C</b> moves config OIDs, one group at a time, out of the in-master handler <b>③</b> and into the framework subagent <b>①</b>, where a GET is answered in-process (~4&nbsp;ms) instead of over the REST loopback.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="center">
    <span class="req"><b>SNMP GET / SET</b> · udp/161</span>
    <div class="drop"></div>
    <div class="node master">
      <div class="name">snmpd — net-snmp master</div>
      <div class="sub">AgentX master · listens tcp:127.0.0.1:705</div>
    </div>
    <div class="router-label">routes by OID — longest-prefix match</div>
    <div class="drop"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="branches">
    <!-- 1 framework subagent -->
    <div class="branch b1">
      <div class="cap"></div>
      <div class="body">
        <div class="top"><span class="num">1</span><h3>Framework subagent</h3></div>
        <div class="where">app_moxa_framework · AgentX</div>
        <span class="tag fast">migrated · fast</span>
        <div class="kv"><span class="k">GET</span>config_operation in-process → ~4&nbsp;ms</div>
        <div class="kv"><span class="k">SET</span>loopback REST PATCH <code>/api/v1/setting/data/…?save</code></div>
        <div class="kv"><span class="k">Serves today</span>
          <span class="oids">system_information · portEvent scalars (reuse from net_*.h)</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 2 ISS subagent -->
    <div class="branch b2">
      <div class="cap"></div>
      <div class="body">
        <div class="top"><span class="num">2</span><h3>ISS subagent</h3></div>
        <div class="where">ISS.exe · AgentX</div>
        <span class="tag native">native register</span>
        <div class="kv"><span class="k">Serves</span>
          <span class="oids">ifTable / ifXTable RO columns, registered by ISS via SNMPRegisterMib</span></div>
        <div class="kv"><span class="k">Note</span><span class="oids">RW columns (ifAdminStatus) stay on ③ — GET forwarded, SET to framework (Plan C)</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 3 in-master ies-auto-mibs -->
    <div class="branch b3">
      <div class="cap"></div>
      <div class="body">
        <div class="top"><span class="num">3</span><h3>ies-auto-mibs</h3></div>
        <div class="where">in-master · libnetsnmpmibs.so</div>
        <span class="tag rest">everything not yet moved</span>
        <div class="rt-wrap">
          <table class="rt">
            <thead><tr><th>condition</th><th>GET</th><th>SET</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="cond">iss_build == 1</td><td class="to-iss">ISS</td><td class="to-fw">framework</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="cond">iss_build == 0</td><td class="to-fw">framework<br><span style="color:var(--ink-soft);font-weight:400">status / config</span></td><td class="to-fw">framework</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="kv"><span class="k">via</span><code>LibFrameworkUri</code> (REST → nginx → actix)</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="callout">
    <span class="arrow">③ → ①</span>
    <p>Design C's migration step: comment a group's <code>MOX_SNMP_INIT_ENTRY</code> (or its dlmod <code>.conf</code>) so the master stops routing it to ③, and register the same OIDs on ① from the shared mapping. GET gets faster; SET stays byte-identical on the existing REST pipeline.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="foot">
    <div>Everything migrated so far is <code>iss_build == 0</code>. The <span class="pin">iss_build == 1</span> row — where a GET must read down into ISS — has not been moved to ① yet.</div>
    <div>Not the end state: ③ stays. The final picture is this hybrid — ① carries the hot config OIDs, ③ keeps serving the rest.</div>
  </div>
</div></div>
